# Installed as /usr/share/lintian/overrides/phpr-server (via
# debian/phpr-server.install). Same justifications as phpr-cli, plus
# the deliberate /var/www/html default.
#
# The default document root /var/www/html is deliberate (see
# README.Debian and the unit's PHPR_DOCROOT): the server refuses to
# start with a non-existent docroot, so a package-owned default is
# needed. This matches long-standing practice of nginx/apache2 in the
# archive and the FHS exception lintian itself documents for /var/www.
phpr-server: dir-or-file-in-var-www [var/www/html/]
# "curl": pure-Rust ureq/rustls crates, no C curl embedded.
phpr-server: embedded-library curl [usr/bin/php-server]
# "libyaml": the unsafe-libyaml Rust crate, not the C libyaml.
phpr-server: embedded-library libyaml [usr/bin/php-server]
